    "template_product_info_columns_NzhHxq": {
      "type": "template--product--info-columns",
      "blocks": {
        "image_and_text_d7H3Dm": {
          "type": "image_and_text",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/suz-headshot.jpg",
            "grid_image_size": "square",
            "heading": "SUZANNE GATT",
            "text": "<p>Founder, CEO</p>",
            "bio_text": "<p>I’m a mom, coach, and 13+ year sports nutrition industry veteran with a career spent building brands, developing products, and bringing sports nutrition to athletes at the highest level.</p><p><strong>But FUTR started with something much more personal.</strong></p><p>For years, parents would ask me the same question: “What can I give my kid?” And despite spending my career inside the sports nutrition industry, I never had an answer I felt great about.</p><p>There were plenty of products for adults. But when it came to young athletes, I kept seeing the same thing: products that weren’t really designed for them, adult formulas repackaged for a younger audience, or options that simply didn’t reflect how kids actually train, play, recover, and grow.</p><p><strong>I knew we could do better. So I decided to build it.</strong></p><p>Over the course of my career, I’ve had the opportunity to work alongside some of the best people in sports nutrition — formulators, researchers, flavor scientists, manufacturers, testing labs, retailers, and industry employees. I’ve seen firsthand what it takes to create great products, but I’ve also learned where shortcuts can happen and which details matter most.</p><p><strong>That means asking harder questions. </strong>Being able to explain why an ingredient is there and why we use the amount we do. Surrounding myself with experts who know more than I do in their respective fields. Choosing partners I trust. And never making a decision simply because it is easier, faster, or looks better on a label.</p><p>I’m still a parent reading the back of the package. I’m still a coach standing on the sideline.&nbsp;</p><p>FUTR is where all the parts of my life come together.</p><p><strong>This one is personal.</strong></p>",
            "bio_secondary_image": "shopify://shop_images/coach-2-_1.jpg",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_text": ""
          }
        },
        "image_and_text_CjEQAK": {
          "type": "image_and_text",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/RAUL_pic.jpg",
            "grid_image_size": "square",
            "heading": "RAUL PUJOL",
            "text": "<p>Partner, Chief Business Development Officer</p>",
            "bio_text": "<p>Raul has played an instrumental role in establishing and developing FUTR from its inception, bringing more than 15 years of experience in the sports nutrition industry and a lifelong passion for athletics, family, and helping young athletes reach their full potential.</p><p>Born in Puerto Rico and raised in Miami, Raul developed his foundation in sports through baseball. He was part of a high school national championship team and later earned Freshman All-American honors while playing college baseball. He holds a Bachelor of Arts degree from Florida International University.</p><p>Throughout his career, Raul has built extensive relationships with athletes, coaches, teams, sports organizations, and leading sports nutrition brands. His experience has provided him with firsthand insight into the role that proper nutrition, quality products, education, and support play in an athlete's development and performance.</p><p>As a husband and father of two boys, Raul's passion for youth athletics extends beyond the game. Grounded in his faith in God, Raul believes in leading with integrity, purpose, and gratitude, values that guide both his family life and professional journey. He understands the dedication, commitment, and support required to help young athletes succeed, as well as the important role parents, coaches, and proper nutrition play throughout their journey.</p><p>At FUTR, Raul leads business development, strategic partnerships, and relationship growth with clubs, leagues, teams, events, and youth sports organizations. He is committed to expanding FUTR's presence in youth sports and making quality sports nutrition, education, and resources more accessible to athletes across every sport and level of competition.</p><p><strong>For partnership or sponsorship opportunities, contact Raul directly at:</strong></p><p>Raul@futrperformance.com</p>",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_text": ""
          }
        },
        "image_and_text_x8Mccy": {
          "type": "image_and_text",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/Angie_-_pic.jpg",
            "grid_image_size": "square",
            "heading": "Angie Pujol ",
            "text": "<p>Partner, Director of Finance Operations</p>",
            "bio_text": "<p>Angie is a lifelong entrepreneur with experience in retail, wholesale, distribution, and the sports nutrition industry. She brings hands-on experience in business operations, sales, and financial management to her role within FUTR. &nbsp;The oldest of ten siblings, Angie grew up in a family of entrepreneurs who modeled hard work, perseverance, and leadership. Her work is grounded in integrity, determination, and a passion for building businesses with purpose.</p><p>As a wife and mother of two athletic boys, Angie understands the commitment behind youth sports and the importance of supporting young athletes through key stages of growth and development. Her family's involvement in athletics makes FUTR's mission deeply personal: expanding access to nutrition education, encouraging healthy eating and regular exercise, and supporting the growth and athletic development of this generation and those to come.</p><p>Beyond her professional work, Angie supports local nonprofits serving children, serves in her church's youth ministry, and is active in several school athletic booster clubs. She brings the same dedication to FUTR, helping young people build a strong foundation for a healthy, active future.</p>",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_text": ""
          }
        },
        "image_and_text_PgNKzt": {
          "type": "image_and_text",
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/jenna.jpg",
            "grid_image_size": "square",
            "heading": "JENNA STANGLAND",
            "text": "<p>MS, RDN, CSSD, LDN, CLT<br/>Director of Athlete Nutrition</p>",
            "bio_text": "<p>Jenna Stangland is a Board Certified Specialist in Sports Dietetics with extensive experience helping athletes use nutrition to support performance, recovery, and long-term development.</p><p>Jenna earned her bachelor’s degree in Genetics and Cell Biology from the University of Minnesota and her master’s degree in Clinical Nutrition, with an emphasis in sports nutrition, from The Ohio State University. Her graduate work included research and athlete education focused on iron absorption, bone health, muscle breakdown and repair, and the role nutrition plays in athletic performance.</p><p>Throughout her career, Jenna has worked with athletes across youth, collegiate, and professional sports. Her experience includes developing the first nutrition program for one of the nation’s largest physician-owned orthopedic organizations, working with elite and youth athletes through CCM hockey camps, supporting collegiate athletic programs, and consulting with sports medicine organizations. She currently serves as Team Dietitian for the Minnesota Timberwolves and Director of Nutrition for the Minnesota Wild organization.</p><p>Jenna also speaks nationally to athletes, parents, coaches, sports dietitians, athletic trainers, and sports medicine professionals on practical, evidence-based approaches to performance nutrition.</p><p><strong>Jenna’s Role at FUTR</strong></p><p>As FUTR’s Director of Athlete Nutrition, Jenna helps shape the nutrition philosophy behind the brand, helping athletes and families better understand not just what to fuel with, but when, why, and how.</p><p>Jenna understand the real-world nutrition challenges young athletes face—from early practices and long tournament days to hydration, fueling, recovery, and demanding school schedules. These insights help shape FUTR’s athlete education, nutrition resources, product guidance, and future innovation.</p><p>She also serves as a trusted nutrition voice for the FUTR community, answering the questions athletes and parents have and turning complex sports nutrition science into clear, actionable guidance they can use every day.</p>",
            "button_link": "",
            "button_text": ""
          }
        },
